<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 512 512'><rect width='512' height='512' rx='96' fill='%230F2A4A'/><rect x='190' y='104' width='196' height='272' rx='22' fill='none' stroke='%23ffffff' stroke-width='30' transform='rotate(14 288 240)'/><rect x='126' y='136' width='196' height='272' rx='22' fill='%23ffffff'/></svg>">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#0c0c12">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <title><%= pageTitle %> | GoGetCards Admin</title>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@400;600;700;800&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/admin.css?v=<%= assetVersion %>">
</head>
<body class="admin-body">
  <%- include('_sidebar') %>
  <main class="admin-main">
    <header class="admin-header">
      <h1 class="admin-header__title"><%= pageTitle %></h1>
      <a href="/admin/products" class="admin-btn">← Back</a>
    </header>
    <div class="admin-content">
      <% if (error) { %>
        <div class="admin-alert admin-alert--error"><%= error %></div>
      <% } %>
      <form method="POST" action="<%= product && product._id ? '/admin/products/' + product._id : '/admin/products' %>" class="admin-form">
        <div class="admin-form__row">
          <div class="form-group"><label>Title *</label><input type="text" name="title" value="<%= product ? product.title : '' %>" required></div>
          <div class="form-group"><label>Slug</label><input type="text" name="slug" value="<%= product ? product.slug : '' %>" placeholder="auto-generated"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="admin-form__row">
          <div class="form-group"><label>Price (USD) *</label><input type="number" step="0.01" name="price" value="<%= product ? (product.price >= 100 ? (product.price / 100).toFixed(2) : product.price) : '' %>" required></div>
          <div class="form-group"><label>Compare Price (USD)</label><input type="number" step="0.01" name="comparePrice" value="<%= product && product.comparePrice ? (product.comparePrice >= 100 ? (product.comparePrice / 100).toFixed(2) : product.comparePrice) : '' %>"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="admin-form__row">
          <div class="form-group"><label>Vendor</label><input type="text" name="vendor" value="<%= product ? product.vendor : '' %>"></div>
          <div class="form-group"><label>Product Type</label><input type="text" name="productType" value="<%= product ? product.productType : '' %>"></div>
        </div>
        <%/* Google Shopping identifiers. All optional and all safe to
             leave blank — every one is omitted from the page and the
             Product schema when empty. Do NOT guess a GTIN: Google
             validates the check digit and resolves it against the real
             product, so a wrong one is a Misrepresentation finding rather
             than a missing field. Copy it off the barcode on the case. */%>
        <fieldset style="border:1px solid var(--admin-border);border-radius:8px;padding:1rem;margin:1rem 0">
          <legend style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:700;padding:0 0.4rem;color:var(--admin-muted)">Google Shopping identifiers (optional)</legend>
          <div class="admin-form__row">
            <div class="form-group"><label>SKU (your own code)</label><input type="text" name="sku" value="<%= product ? (product.sku || '') : '' %>" placeholder="ZTCG-OP17-BB"></div>
            <div class="form-group"><label>GTIN / barcode</label><input type="text" name="gtin" value="<%= product ? (product.gtin || '') : '' %>" placeholder="Copy off the barcode. Leave blank if unknown."></div>
          </div>
          <div class="admin-form__row">
            <div class="form-group"><label>MPN (manufacturer part no.)</label><input type="text" name="mpn" value="<%= product ? (product.mpn || '') : '' %>"></div>
            <div class="form-group"><label>Brand (manufacturer)</label><input type="text" name="brand" value="<%= product ? (product.brand || '') : '' %>" placeholder="Defaults to Vendor"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="admin-form__row">
            <div class="form-group"><label>Language</label><input type="text" name="language" value="<%= product ? (product.language === undefined ? 'English' : product.language) : 'English' %>" placeholder="English"></div>
            <div class="form-group"><label>Edition</label><input type="text" name="edition" value="<%= product ? (product.edition || '') : '' %>" placeholder="1st Edition"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="form-group"><label>Set code</label><input type="text" name="setCode" value="<%= product ? (product.setCode || '') : '' %>" placeholder="OP-17"></div>
        </fieldset>
        <%/* Variant grouping. One manufactured item that arrives as two or
             more boxes — Day and Night, an alternate cover, a regional
             printing.

             EACH BOX IS ITS OWN PRODUCT HERE. Create one per box, give
             them the SAME group id and DIFFERENT names, and the storefront
             grows a Version chooser between them while the feed sends them
             to Google as variants of one item rather than as two listings
             fighting over the same barcode.

             That last part is the reason this exists: two boxes of one
             item share a GTIN and an MPN, and Google reads two ungrouped
             offers with the same GTIN as the same listing sent twice — it
             keeps one and drops the other. */%>
        <fieldset style="border:1px solid var(--admin-border);border-radius:8px;padding:1rem;margin:1rem 0">
          <legend style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:700;padding:0 0.4rem;color:var(--admin-muted)">Variant group (optional)</legend>
          <p style="margin:0 0 0.75rem;font-size:0.74rem;color:var(--admin-muted);line-height:1.5">
            For one product sold as several boxes. Create a product per box, give every one the
            <strong>same group id</strong> and a <strong>different version name</strong>. The name is added
            to the title automatically — type the base title only.
          </p>
          <div class="admin-form__row">
            <div class="form-group">
              <label>Group id</label>
              <input type="text" name="variantGroup" maxlength="50" value="<%= product ? (product.variantGroup || '') : '' %>" placeholder="10-10448-120">
              <small style="color:var(--admin-muted);font-size:0.72rem">Any stable string, identical across the group. The manufacturer's item number is the natural choice.</small>
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
              <label>Version name</label>
              <input type="text" name="variantName" maxlength="100" value="<%= product ? (product.variantName || '') : '' %>" placeholder="Night (Umbreon ex)">
              <small style="color:var(--admin-muted);font-size:0.72rem">Appended to the title as “Base — Night (Umbreon ex)”. Must differ from every other box in the group.</small>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="admin-form__row">
            <div class="form-group">
              <label>Tells the versions apart by</label>
              <select name="variantAxis">
                <% (typeof variantAxes !== 'undefined' ? variantAxes : []).forEach(function (a) { %>
                <%/* A NEW product has no `product` at all, so the check has
                     to fall back to the default axis rather than to false —
                     otherwise the form opens with nothing selected, the
                     browser silently submits the first option, and which
                     axis that is depends on the order of the list. */%>
                  <option value="<%= a.id %>" <%= ((product && product.variantAxis) || 'color') === a.id ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= a.label %></option>
                <% }); %>
              </select>
              <small style="color:var(--admin-muted);font-size:0.72rem">Google reads a fixed set of attributes here. Every box in a group must use the same one.</small>
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
              <label>Order in the chooser</label>
              <input type="number" name="variantOrder" value="<%= product ? (product.variantOrder || 0) : 0 %>">
              <small style="color:var(--admin-muted);font-size:0.72rem">Lowest first. Ties fall back to the version name.</small>
            </div>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
        <div class="form-group"><label>Image URL</label><input type="text" name="imageUrl" value="<%= product ? product.imageUrl : '' %>" placeholder="https://..."></div>
        <div class="form-group"><label>Additional Images (one URL per line)</label><textarea name="images" rows="3"><%= product && product.images ? product.images.join('\n') : '' %></textarea></div>
        <div class="form-group"><label>Description (HTML)</label><textarea name="description" rows="6"><%= product ? product.description : '' %></textarea></div>
        <%
          /* On a validation-error re-render, `product` is the raw req.body, so
             `specs` arrives as the textarea string rather than a parsed array.
             Handle both so the admin never loses what they typed. */
          var specsValue = '';
          if (product && product.specs) {
            specsValue = Array.isArray(product.specs)
              ? product.specs.map(function (s) { return s.label + ': ' + s.value; }).join('\n')
              : String(product.specs);
          }
        %>
        <div class="form-group">
          <label>Specifications (one "Label: Value" per line)</label>
          <select id="spec-template-picker" style="margin-bottom:8px">
            <option value="">Start from a template…</option>
            <% (typeof specTemplates !== 'undefined' ? specTemplates : []).forEach(function (t) { %>
              <option value="<%= t.id %>"><%= t.label %></option>
            <% }); %>
          </select>
          <textarea id="spec-textarea" name="specs" rows="5" placeholder="Configuration: 24 Booster Packs&#10;Cards Per Pack: 12&#10;Language: English"><%= specsValue %></textarea>
          <small style="display:block;margin-top:6px;opacity:0.6">Templates only prefill these rows — edit them freely afterwards, and always check pack counts against the distributor sheet, since publishers vary them per set.</small>
        </div>
        <script>
          (function () {
            var TEMPLATES = <%- jsonForScript(typeof specTemplates !== 'undefined' ? specTemplates : []) %>;
            var picker = document.getElementById('spec-template-picker');
            var box = document.getElementById('spec-textarea');
            if (!picker || !box) return;
            picker.addEventListener('change', function () {
              var tpl = TEMPLATES.filter(function (t) { return t.id === picker.value; })[0];
              if (!tpl) return;
              if (box.value.trim() && !window.confirm('Replace the current specifications with the "' + tpl.label + '" template?')) {
                picker.value = '';
                return;
              }
              box.value = tpl.specs.map(function (s) { return s.label + ': ' + s.value; }).join('\n');
              picker.value = '';
            });
          })();
        </script>
        <div class="admin-form__row">
          <div class="form-group"><label>Collections (comma-separated)</label><input type="text" name="collections" value="<%= product && product.collections ? product.collections.join(', ') : '' %>"></div>
          <div class="form-group"><label>Tags (comma-separated)</label><input type="text" name="tags" value="<%= product && product.tags ? product.tags.join(', ') : '' %>"></div>
        </div>
<%/* Shopify Variant ID and Custom Checkout URL used to sit here. Both are
     gone from the form: the variant id was only ever a manual seed for the
     rotator, which resolves variants itself, and the checkout URL override
     is no longer used by any product. The schema fields remain so live
     checkout keeps working for anything that still carries a value — see
     the comment in models/Product.js. Because the save handler passes a
     plain object to findByIdAndUpdate, which mongoose treats as $set,
     removing them here leaves existing values untouched rather than
     silently blanking them. */%>
        <div class="admin-form__row">
          <div class="form-group"><label>Stock</label><input type="number" name="stock" value="<%= product ? product.stock : 0 %>"></div>
          <div class="form-group">
            <label>Badge</label>
            <select name="badge">
              <option value="">None</option>
              <% ['Hot', 'Limited', 'Preorder', 'Rare', 'New'].forEach(function(b) { %>
                <option value="<%= b %>" <%= product && product.badge === b ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= b %></option>
              <% }); %>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="admin-form__row">
          <div class="form-group"><label>Allocation Limit (0=unlimited)</label><input type="number" name="allocationLimit" value="<%= product ? (product.allocationLimit || 0) : 0 %>"></div>
          <div class="form-group"><label>Preorder Ships (display text)</label><input type="text" name="preorderShips" value="<%= product ? (product.preorderShips || '') : '' %>" placeholder="Q2 2026"></div>
        </div>
        <%/* The real release date, as a date. "Q2 2026" is fine for a
             shopper and useless to a crawler, so schema.org
             availabilityDate is built from THIS field and never from the
             free text above. Merchant Center accepts a preorder only when
             the listing says when the item becomes available, so a
             preorder without this competes as though it were mislabelled
             in-stock product. */%>
        <div class="admin-form__row">
          <div class="form-group">
            <label>Release date (preorders)</label>
            <input type="date" name="releaseDate" value="<%= product && product.releaseDate ? new Date(product.releaseDate).toISOString().split('T')[0] : '' %>">
            <small style="color:var(--admin-muted);font-size:0.72rem">Drives the release date shown on the page and Google's availabilityDate. Set it on every preorder.</small>
          </div>
          <div class="form-group"></div>
        </div>
        <%/* ── Prices in other markets ────────────────────────────────
             One row per market. A BLANK ROW MEANS NOT SOLD THERE — not
             "convert it", not "use the US price". That is the whole rule:
             the market's URL 404s, the market's feed omits the product,
             and nothing anywhere quotes a number the checkout cannot
             charge. Filling one in is what opens the product in that
             market.

             Enter the amount the customer pays, in that currency's
             smallest unit: cents for CAD and EUR, pence for GBP, whole
             yen for JPY. UK and EU prices include VAT, because consumer
             prices there must. */%>
        <% var _otherMarkets = (typeof allMarkets !== 'undefined' ? allMarkets : []).filter(function (m) { return !m.isDefault; }); %>
        <% if (_otherMarkets.length) { %>
        <fieldset style="border:1px solid var(--admin-border);border-radius:8px;padding:1rem;margin:1rem 0">
          <legend style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:700;padding:0 0.4rem;color:var(--admin-muted)">Prices in other markets</legend>
          <p style="font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--admin-muted);margin:0 0 0.85rem;line-height:1.6">
            Leave blank to not sell this product in that market. Enter the price the way you would
            write it &mdash; <strong>179.99</strong>, not 17999 &mdash; and it is what the customer is
            charged: the same figure goes on the page, in the structured data and in that market's
            Google feed. UK and EU prices include VAT, because consumer prices there must.
          </p>
          <% _otherMarkets.forEach(function (m) { %>
            <% var _row = ((product && product.marketPrices) || []).find(function (r) { return String(r.market).toUpperCase() === m.id; }) || {}; %>
            <div class="admin-form__row" style="align-items:flex-end">
              <div class="form-group" style="max-width:9rem">
                <label><%- include('../partials/flag', { code: m.id, label: m.name, size: 16 }) %> <%= m.id %> price <span style="color:var(--admin-muted)">(<%= m.currency %>)</span></label>
                <input type="number" min="0" step="0.01" name="mp_<%= m.id %>_amount"
                       value="<%= _row.amount ? (_row.amount / 100).toFixed(2) : '' %>" placeholder="blank = not sold">
              </div>
              <div class="form-group" style="max-width:9rem">
                <label>Compare at</label>
                <input type="number" min="0" step="0.01" name="mp_<%= m.id %>_compare"
                       value="<%= _row.compareAmount ? (_row.compareAmount / 100).toFixed(2) : '' %>">
              </div>
              <div class="form-group">
                <label style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.45rem;margin-top:1.4rem">
                  <input type="checkbox" name="mp_<%= m.id %>_available" <%= _row.available === false ? '' : 'checked' %>>
                  On sale in <%= m.id %>
                </label>
              </div>
            </div>
          <% }); %>
        </fieldset>
        <% } %>

        <%/* ── Listed but unbuyable ──────────────────────────────────
             Deliberately its own block rather than another checkbox in the
             row below, because it is not the same kind of switch: it keeps
             a page advertising an item the checkout will refuse, and the
             buyer only finds out after typing their address. The warning
             is on the screen so nobody turns it on thinking it means
             "sold out". */%>
        <div class="form-group" style="border:1px solid var(--admin-border-2);border-radius:10px;padding:1rem 1.1rem;margin:1.25rem 0;">
          <label style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.55rem;margin:0;">
            <input type="checkbox" name="stockHold" <%= product && product.stockHold ? 'checked' : '' %>>
            Stock hold — keep listed as available, refuse at the payment step
          </label>
          <small style="display:block;color:var(--admin-muted);font-size:0.72rem;margin-top:0.5rem;line-height:1.6">
            The page, the structured data <em>and the Google feed</em> keep saying in stock; the
            buyer is stopped one step before payment and offered the replacement below. Nothing
            is charged. Because the feed still advertises it, expect Merchant Center to treat this
            as an availability misrepresentation if it notices — that is an action against the
            account, not the listing.
            <strong>To genuinely sell out an item, untick Available instead</strong> — that reports
            out of stock to Google, refuses at the start of checkout, and is what the sold-out
            badge reads.
          </small>
          <label style="display:block;margin-top:0.85rem;">Replace with (slug)</label>
          <input type="text" name="supersededBy" placeholder="one-piece-card-game-op-18-booster-box-24-packs-factory-sealed-english"
                 value="<%= product ? (product.supersededBy || '') : '' %>">
          <small style="color:var(--admin-muted);font-size:0.72rem">
            Offered by name at the refusal. Must be available and not itself held, or the buyer
            is sent to the catalogue instead.
          </small>
        </div>
        <div class="admin-form__checks">
          <label><input type="checkbox" name="available" <%= product && product.available ? 'checked' : '' %>> Available</label>
          <label><input type="checkbox" name="preorder" <%= product && product.preorder ? 'checked' : '' %>> Preorder</label>
          <label><input type="checkbox" name="featured" <%= product && product.featured ? 'checked' : '' %>> Featured</label>
        </div>
        <button type="submit" class="admin-btn admin-btn--primary"><%= product && product._id ? 'Update Product' : 'Create Product' %></button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
